<http://data.silknow.org/object/bae6c175-c328-39e5-89d5-0dd48bbac0c1/observation/5>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nThis mantua and petticoat represent the grandest style of court dress. The skirt made it necessary for the wearer to go sideways through doors, but had the advantage of displaying a large area of lavish decoration. Botanically accurate flowers were a feature of Rococo embroidery, patterned silks and printed textiles of the 1740s and 1750s in England. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/bae6c175-c328-39e5-89d5-0dd48bbac0c1> .

